These papers describe Nano-11, a plant-derived, dendrimer-like α-D-glucan nanoparticle, as an effective vaccine adjuvant. Nano-11, with a positive surface charge, enhances antigen uptake and activates dendritic cells (DCs), promoting expression of costimulatory molecules (CD80, CD86) and IL-1β secretion. In vivo, it significantly boosts antibody responses to protein antigens, comparable to aluminum hydroxide. Nano-11 induces a transient local inflammatory response, clearing gradually over weeks, and targets antigens to migratory DCs in draining lymph nodes. Its favorable safety profile and efficacy make it a promising adjuvant candidate.

